\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Surface-runoff hydrograph under maximum 30-minute intensity ($I_{30}$) of 60~mm/h for the three soil profiles. The Plinthosol (effective saturated hydraulic conductivity 0.50~cm/h) reaches steady state in less than 10~minutes, while the Ferralsol (8.0~cm/h) generates no runoff at any point during the 60-minute event.}}{26}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hidrograma}{{9}{26}{Surface-runoff hydrograph under maximum 30-minute intensity ($I_{30}$) of 60~mm/h for the three soil profiles. The Plinthosol (effective saturated hydraulic conductivity 0.50~cm/h) reaches steady state in less than 10~minutes, while the Ferralsol (8.0~cm/h) generates no runoff at any point during the 60-minute event}{figure.9}{}}
